Package: zlinuxdocs
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Architecture: all
Maintainer: zlinuxdocs contributors <noreply@github.com>
Section: text
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-lxml, poppler-utils
Recommends: qpdf, libreoffice-writer
Description: inspect, repair, convert and validate .docx document sets
 zlinuxdocs is a command-line tool for people who are sent Word documents and
 have to turn them into PDFs that will not be handed back at the counter.
 .
 It reports what is really inside a .docx (headings, styles, tables, sections,
 verification markers); repairs documents whose headings only LOOK like
 headings, so the exported PDF gains a real clickable chapter list; converts to
 PDF through LibreOffice with bookmarks and a searchable text layer; and checks
 the resulting PDF, exiting non-zero when it is not fit to send.
 .
 Commands:
  inspect       say what is really inside a Word document
  fix-headings  turn look-alike headings into real headings (idempotent)
  convert       make a PDF with a working chapter list (needs LibreOffice)
  validate      check a PDF is fit to send; exits non-zero when it is not
  markers       list the [V] verification marks a reviewer left behind
  profile       show or export the house print settings
 .
 Also installed as the short name "zld". Run "zlinuxdocs quickstart" for a
 five-command walkthrough against the example documents that ship with it.
 .
 PDF/A conformance is NOT claimed. The optional --pdfa flag asks LibreOffice
 for an archival flavour but nothing here can verify conformance; that needs a
 dedicated validator such as veraPDF.
 .
 Works entirely offline. Makes no network connections and collects no
 telemetry. Installs no maintainer scripts: it is a plain file drop.
Homepage: https://github.com/zexp1/zlinuxdocs
